    {
      "id": "m-schedule",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "stress": [],
      "answerable": true,
      "refused": false,
      "forbidden_hit": false,
      "keyword_score": 1.0,
      "section_hit": true,
      "grounded": true,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "passed": true,
      "latency_s": 4.476214899999945,
      "answer_text": "The learning-rate schedule is explicitly described in the [optimizer] section. It follows the formula:  \n**lrate = d<sup>-0.5</sup> \u00b7 min(step_num<sup>-0.5</sup>, step_num \u00b7 warmup_steps<sup>-1.5</sup>)**,  \nwhere **warmup_steps = 4000**. This schedule increases the learning rate **linearly** for the first **4000 steps** (warmup phase) and then **decreases it proportionally to the inverse square root of the step number** thereafter.  \n\nThe paper explicitly states this is a **measured and implemented schedule** used in their training regime. No projections or citations are involved.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "section": "optimizer",
          "chunk_id": "1706.03762v7_optimizer_0"
        },
