      "answer_text": "The paper states that during inference, they used a beam size of 4 and a length penalty \u03b1 = 0.6 for both the English-to-German and English-to-French translation tasks (machine translation sections). For the English constituency parsing task, they used a beam size of 21 and \u03b1 = 0.3 for both the WSJ-only and semi-supervised settings (English constituency parsing sections).",
