      "passed": true,
      "latency_s": 5.32136909999997,
      "answer_text": "Yes, the authors experimented with using learned positional embeddings instead of sinusoidal ones (Positional Encoding). They found that the two versions produced nearly identical results, as indicated in Table 3 row (E) (Model Variations). Specifically, the learned positional embeddings yielded a BLEU score of 25.7, which is the same as the sinusoidal version (Model Variations). The paper implies that the choice between sinusoidal and learned positional embeddings does not significantly impact model performance, though it isn't stated directly. The authors ultimately chose the sinusoidal version because it may allow the model to extrapolate to sequence lengths longer than those encountered during training (Positional Encoding).",
