      "answer_text": "The evidence does not explicitly state that the authors chose learned positional embeddings for their final model. Instead, it mentions that they experimented with both learned positional embeddings and sinusoidal positional encodings, finding that the two versions produced nearly identical results (see Table 3 row (E)) (Model Variations). The authors ultimately chose the sinusoidal version because it may allow the model to extrapolate to sequence lengths longer than those encountered during training (Positional Encoding). \n\nThus, the evidence does not support the claim that learned positional embeddings were chosen for the final model. Instead, it indicates that sinusoidal positional encodings were selected for their potential extrapolation benefits.",
